<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Set up your initializer after installation.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Steps",
      subtitle: "Follow these steps to configure the gem in your app.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Open <span class="font-mono">config/initializers/recording_studio_ai.rb</span>.</li>
      <li>Paste the initializer template below and adjust values for your environment.</li>
      <li>Add provider API keys and choose the profile/fallback strategy you want to support.</li>
      <li>Restart the app so initializer changes are loaded.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Initializer example",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @config_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Configuration parameters",
      subtitle: "Every setting you can put in the initializer, with defaults.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Table::Component.new(data: @config_options) do |table| %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Param",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:key], class: "font-mono text-xs") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Required", html: ->(option) { option[:required] }) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Possible values", html: ->(option) { option[:accepted_values] }) %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Default",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:default], class: "font-mono text-xs break-all") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Description", html: ->(option) { option[:explanation] }) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "1. Add a Provider",
      subtitle: "Providers are single adapter classes (for example OpenAI and Gemini). Each provider is one class under lib/recording_studio_ai/providers/<provider>.rb.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Create a provider class under <span class="font-mono">lib/recording_studio_ai/providers/&lt;provider&gt;.rb</span> that inherits <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI::Providers::Base</span> and declares <span class="font-mono">provider_key</span>.</li>
      <li>Implement <span class="font-mono">#generate</span>. Add <span class="font-mono">#stream</span> only when models stream, and <span class="font-mono">#submit_batch</span> / <span class="font-mono">#refresh_batch</span> / <span class="font-mono">#cancel_batch</span> only when they batch. Apps call <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.generate</span> (pass <span class="font-mono">stream: true</span> to stream) and the batch methods — not <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.stream</span>.</li>
      <li>Add credentials the same way as OpenAI and Gemini: <span class="font-mono">config.&lt;provider_key&gt;_api_key</span> and optional <span class="font-mono">config.&lt;provider_key&gt;_client</span>. <span class="font-mono">configured?</span> is shared on the base class.</li>
      <li>Register it from the host initializer or another gem's engine initializer with <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.register_provider(:key, instance)</span>.</li>
      <li>Optionally set <span class="font-mono">config.discovery_enabled = true</span> to auto-register provider classes found under the providers path.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "my_provider.rb",
    snippets: [
      { label: "my_provider.rb", language: "ruby", code: @provider_class_example },
      { label: "Initializer", language: "ruby", code: @provider_initializer_example }
    ]
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Provider registration examples",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @provider_extension_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "2. Add a Model",
      subtitle: "Models are declarative registration scripts (no class). Built-ins ship with the gem; add your own the same way.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Pick the provider the model belongs to (it must be registered first).</li>
      <li>Create a registration file. For gem-style catalogs use <span class="font-mono">lib/recording_studio_ai/models/&lt;provider-key&gt;/&lt;model-key&gt;.rb</span> (for example <span class="font-mono">models/openai/gpt-5-mini.rb</span>, <span class="font-mono">models/gemini/gemini-2-5-pro.rb</span>). For a host app, any initializer works.</li>
      <li>The file/key is a lowercase hyphenated slug (dots become hyphens); the <span class="font-mono">model:</span> value is the exact provider API model string used in profiles.</li>
      <li>Call <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.models.register(...)</span> and declare <span class="font-mono">delivery</span>, <span class="font-mono">parameters</span>, <span class="font-mono">tools</span>, and <span class="font-mono">modalities</span> so the resolver and AI playground know what the model supports.</li>
      <li>Pass <span class="font-mono">override: true</span> to replace an existing model for the same provider and key.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Model registration",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @model_registration_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "3. Create Profiles",
      subtitle: "Profiles are ordered preference lists of provider/model candidates used by generate (including stream: true) and batch.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Set <span class="font-mono">config.profiles</span> in <span class="font-mono">config/initializers/recording_studio_ai.rb</span>.</li>
      <li>Reference each model by its provider API model string (the <span class="font-mono">model:</span> value from registration). Do not repeat capabilities here — they come from the model registry.</li>
      <li>Order candidates by preference; the resolver picks the first configured provider whose model supports the request.</li>
      <li>Set <span class="font-mono">config.default_profile</span> and, optionally, <span class="font-mono">config.profile_fallbacks</span> for tier fallback.</li>
      <li>For a one-off hop list that skips profiles, pass <span class="font-mono">fallbacks:</span> on <span class="font-mono">generate</span>. Each entry needs <span class="font-mono">provider</span> and <span class="font-mono">model</span>; you may also set hop-only params such as <span class="font-mono">temperature</span>, <span class="font-mono">verbosity</span>, <span class="font-mono">max_output_tokens</span>, or <span class="font-mono">reasoning_effort</span>. Top-level caller overrides still win.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Profile configuration",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @profile_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Create Custom Tools",
      subtitle: "Register a tool and pass it to generate. Streaming uses the same call with stream: true.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Define a stable key and version for your tool.</li>
      <li>Provide clear parameter schema and usage guidance.</li>
      <li>Implement a deterministic executor that returns serializable data.</li>
      <li>Pass the tool reference in the request's custom_tools array.</li>
      <li>Pass <span class="font-mono">override: true</span> to replace an existing tool with the same key and version.</li>
    </ol>

    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Tool registration fields",
      subtitle: "Every argument RecordingStudioAI.tools.register accepts.",
      variant: :h4,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Table::Component.new(data: @custom_tool_options) do |table| %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Param",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:key], class: "font-mono text-xs") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Required", html: ->(option) { option[:required] }) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Possible values", html: ->(option) { option[:accepted_values] }) %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Default",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:default], class: "font-mono text-xs break-all") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Description", html: ->(option) { option[:explanation] }) %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Argument fields inside parameters",
      subtitle: "Each item in the parameters array can set these keys.",
      variant: :h4,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Table::Component.new(data: @custom_tool_parameter_options) do |table| %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Param",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:key], class: "font-mono text-xs") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Required", html: ->(option) { option[:required] }) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Possible values", html: ->(option) { option[:accepted_values] }) %>
      <% table.column(
        title: "Default",
        html: ->(option) { content_tag(:span, option[:default], class: "font-mono text-xs break-all") }
      ) %>
      <% table.column(title: "Description", html: ->(option) { option[:explanation] }) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Custom tool registration and usage",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @custom_tools_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Registry overrides",
      subtitle: "Replace a registered model, tool, or prompt. Prompts can also lock replacement with overridable: false.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li><span class="font-mono">override: true</span> on <span class="font-mono">models.register</span>, <span class="font-mono">tools.register</span>, and <span class="font-mono">prompts.register</span> replaces the existing entry with the same identity.</li>
      <li>Models are keyed by provider + key. Tools and prompts are keyed by key + version.</li>
      <li>Prompts also take <span class="font-mono">overridable: true|false</span> (default true). A later <span class="font-mono">override: true</span> only succeeds when the existing prompt is overridable.</li>
      <li>Call sites keep using the same key — no change to <span class="font-mono">generate</span> or <span class="font-mono">prompt(...).call</span>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Override models, tools, and prompts",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @registry_overrides_example
  ) %>
</div>
